From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:07:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: apple,s8000-display-pipe: Add the eDP
 transmitter and panel supply

On the A9, iOS switches the panel off whenever the display sleeps: the
DisplayPort driver drops the panel's supply (the Apple device tree's
function-lcd_ldo on the displayport node) and trains the eDP link again
when it comes back. Allow the DisplayPort transmitter's register window as
a last "dp" region, the panel supply as apple,lcd-ldo-gpios and the
panel's backlight, so the display pipe's driver can do the same in system
sleep. The A10's pipe gets the same optional window and properties: its
DisplayPort block and supply are not described yet, but nothing points to
a different scheme there.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Link: https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard/pull/231#issuecomment-7138590680
---
 .../display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml     | 25 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml
index 103344b..43d3e54 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml
@@ -34,16 +34,31 @@ properties:
 
   reg:
     minItems: 3
-    maxItems: 8
+    maxItems: 9
 
   reg-names:
     minItems: 3
-    maxItems: 8
+    maxItems: 9
 
   interrupts:
     minItems: 5
     maxItems: 6
 
+  apple,lcd-ldo-gpios:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      The panel supply enable (the Apple device tree's function-lcd_ldo on
+      the displayport node). With it, the panel is switched off in system
+      sleep and the eDP link is trained again on wake over the DisplayPort
+      transmitter's AUX channel (the "dp" register window), leaving the pipe
+      and the transmitter as the bootloader set them.
+
+  backlight:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description:
+      The panel's backlight, which must stay off until the panel is back
+      after a wake.
+
   power-domains:
     minItems: 2
     maxItems: 3
@@ -80,17 +95,21 @@ allOf:
     then:
       properties:
         reg:
+          minItems: 3
           items:
             - description:
                 ADP window, with the control and interrupt registers, the
                 parameter FIFO port and the pipe layer registers
             - description: Display DART (dart-disp0), first window
             - description: Display DART (dart-disp0), second window
+            - description: DisplayPort transmitter (displayport)
         reg-names:
+          minItems: 3
           items:
             - const: adp
             - const: dart0
             - const: dart1
+            - const: dp
         interrupts:
           items:
             - description:
@@ -121,6 +140,7 @@ allOf:
             - description: Seven-register side block
             - description: Display DART (dart-disp0), first window
             - description: Display DART (dart-disp0), second window
+            - description: DisplayPort transmitter (displayport)
 
         reg-names:
           minItems: 6
@@ -133,6 +153,7 @@ allOf:
             - const: side
             - const: dart0
             - const: dart1
+            - const: dp
 
         interrupts:
           items:
